<title>FRANCE: Jospin letters say deficit must be read as trend.</title>
<headline>Jospin letters say deficit must be read as trend.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin's budget instruction letters to ministers do not contain numbers on public deficits and say the Maastricht Treaty deficit criterion must be read in terms of a trend, Jospin's office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Jospin's spokesman told reporters the letters highlighted that fighting unemployment was the &quot;absolute priority&quot;, but that this had to be done while respecting France's European Union commitments on the public deficit.</p>
<p>Jospin said the &quot;respect for European commitments&quot; on the deficit should in any case be read in terms of the trend, the spokesman added.</p>
</text>
